<p><sup><a id="fn.1" href="#fnr.1">1</a></sup> : My simple words here are too simple. There is a lot going on behind the scenes, and I don&rsquo;t have a good grasp of it yet myself, actually. Learning in progress. IndieAuth is based on OAuth, which is the commercial brand that usually comes with OpenID, which is all the &ldquo;sign in with Google/Apple/Facebook/Whatever&rdquo; stuff you usually see.</p>
<p><sup><a id="fn.2" href="#fnr.2">2</a></sup> : See the above, same here. There&rsquo;s an A record and a CNAME record when you register a domain, and I remember I knew more about them at one point when I registered the domain. A record points to the actual IP, and a CNAME points to a subdomain (the www, but it can also be blog.website.com, or whatever you&rsquo;d like).</p>
